  "account-endpoint-healthchecks": {
    "body": {
      "check_type": "icmp",
      "endpoint": "203.0.113.1",
      "name": "dp-roundtrip-hc"
    },
    "path": "/accounts/{}/diagnostics/endpoint-healthchecks",
    "why": "Body corrected 2026-07-28 from Cloudflare's OWN published schema (components.schemas.magic-transit_endpoint_health_check): the required fields are check_type and endpoint, and check_type is an enum whose only member is icmp. The previous body sent target and type, which are not fields of this endpoint at all, so all six shapes tried across two sittings were guessing at the wrong names. The schema was vendored in this repo the whole time and nobody read it. With the schema-shaped body the endpoint STILL answers a bare 1002 Invalid request naming no field. That no longer implicates our body, which is what changed: the schema is magic-transit and this account has no Magic Transit. Recorded as unknown rather than as an entitlement, because Cloudflare has not said so and this campaign has twice turned an assumed entitlement into a defect of ours."
  },
