  "device-policy-default": {
    "body": null,
    "path": "/accounts/{}/devices/policy",
    "why": "NO CREATE, deliberately. This surface is a SINGLETON: the registry reads one object from /accounts/{}/devices/policy and writes it with writeSingleObject PATCH, and it is already proven by test/live-cf-singleton-prove.ts. A POST to the same path does not create the thing this surface represents, it creates a SECOND device settings policy beside the default, which the surface would never capture and a restore would never put back. The synthesised body also filled `match` with a random string, and Cloudflare answered 'invalid wirefilter expression'; supplying a valid expression would have made the create succeed and proved the wrong thing, leaving a stray policy on the account. Reported as CREATE-REFUSED it looked like work owed, which is why this is recorded rather than simply removed."
  },
