  "dlp-data-classes": {
    "body": {
      "name": "dp-roundtrip-dataclass",
      "expression": "http.host eq \"dp-probe.invalid\"",
      "data_tags": [],
      "sensitivity_levels": [
        {
          "group_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
          "level_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"
        }
      ]
    },
    "path": "/accounts/{}/dlp/data_classes",
    "why": "The body is now WELL FORMED and the refusal is Forbidden, an entitlement, which is the true reason. It previously carried synthesised placeholders where UUIDs belong, so Cloudflare refused it at JSON parsing and the recorded reason was OUR malformed request, which never reached the entitlement check. The group ids are deliberately well-formed UUIDs that do not exist: real ones cannot be obtained, because the account holds no sensitivity groups and creating one is itself Forbidden. Two required fields were found by asking (the endpoint named `data_tags` and `sensitivity_levels` in turn) rather than guessed."
  },
