  "dlp-profiles-custom": {
    "body": {
      "name": "dp-roundtrip-profile",
      "description": "dp roundtrip",
      "allowed_match_count": 1,
      "entries": [
        {
          "enabled": false,
          "name": "dp-entry",
          "pattern": {
            "regex": "dp-[0-9]{4}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "path": "/accounts/{}/dlp/profiles/custom",
    "why": "Body corrected 2026-07-28 from Cloudflare's published schema. The previous body wrapped the profile in a `profiles` array, and the schema says the request body IS the profile object: required `name`, with entries/description/allowed_match_count alongside it. So the recorded 3314 Forbidden was reached with a body that would have failed schema validation anyway, which is the confounding this campaign has been caught by twice. DLP is a paid Zero Trust product and the corrected body is still refused, so the entitlement reading stands, but it now stands on evidence rather than on a request that never got that far."
  },
